  _id: 14041214
  _key: DIALOGUE_SERAPHINE_NODE_Q2_COMPLETION
  _displayName: 
  _description: 
  _speakerName: Seraphine
  _dialogueSegments:
  - The darkness surrounding the Eastern Altar... it has finally begun to fade.
  - 'So it is done. Aurelian''s suffering has come to an end.

    For so long, I
    feared that facing him would mean abandoning the last hope of saving my brother.'
  - Perhaps there was never a way to restore what he had lost.
  - But you gave me the courage to face the truth, and for that I shall always be
    grateful.
  - 'There is something I wish to entrust to you. A weapon I have carried since the
    days of our order.

    May it serve you better than it served me.'
  _dialogueText: 'The darkness surrounding the Eastern Altar... it has finally begun
    to fade.

    So it is done. Aurelian''s suffering has come to an end.

    For
    so long, I feared that facing him would mean abandoning the last hope of saving
    my brother.

    Perhaps there was never a way to restore what he had lost.

    But
    you gave me the courage to face the truth, and for that I shall always be grateful.

    There
    is something I wish to entrust to you. A weapon I have carried since the days
    of our order.

    May it serve you better than it served me.'
  _choices:
  - _choiceText: I'll carry it with honour.
